@seb-odoo I would prefer not to add an option to the public API of the action service. There're alternatives, which would work for your issue:
- toggle a flag in the closure
```js
keepDialogs = true;
restore();

function restore() {
    const shouldKeepDialogs = keepDialogs;
    keepDialogs = false;
}
```
- have a private `_restore` function which takes the option, but the public `restore` doesn't
- automatically keep dialogs in `restore` (I tried [here](https://github.com/odoo-dev/odoo/commit/e6f348f4cec87f4890a585afb11ffb4dce559cc2), it was green). That kind of makes sense, because we close dialogs typically for "moving forward" flows (typically, click on a view button). And when you do that from a dialog, you don't want to see the action being executed in the background with the dialog remaining open in top. However, in restore, we're rather moving backward (typically clicking on the breadcrumbs).

For the record, I always experimented with rejecting the promise _after_ the current controller has been restored [[1]](https://github.com/odoo-dev/odoo/commit/334e082af77ca0370e8842bb61e3cd319cb4f01e). It's green as well, modulo a few tests to adapt. However, I'm not really confident with this, and the failing tests indicated a real drawback: if the restored controller fails as well (i.e. 2 errors are thrown), only one is actually displayed, as we never reach the `reject()` code for the first error.

What do you think?
cc @jpp-odoo

